    "Existence of an interference": "The applicants’ freedom of expression was interfered with through multiple State measures targeting the Anti-Corruption Foundation (FBK) and its associated entities. The freezing of bank accounts, including those of the applicants’ relatives, prevented the FBK from paying salaries or continuing its anti-corruption investigative work and online publishing activities (see paragraph 19). Widespread searches and seizures of computers, mobile phones and production equipment across the applicants’ offices and homes, as well as those of their relatives, disrupted their ability to create and disseminate content (see paragraphs 24-26). The designation of the FBK as a “foreign agent” imposed operational restrictions and stigma (see paragraph 29), while the subsequent designation of the FBK, the Foundation for the Defence of Civil Rights (FZPG) and the Navalnyy Headquarters as “extremist” organisations, followed by their dissolution and prohibition, effectively silenced their anti-corruption messaging (see paragraph 35). These measures directly obstructed the applicants’ exercise of their right to freedom of expression under Article 10.",

